; main.c:10121
MSG_35BE063F (901645887//)
AmigaMCE plays music from a Plex Media Server on your network: its music libraries, by artist and album, with their covers. The server makes each track an MP3 this Amiga can play: 22kHz mono for a 68020/030, 24kHz stereo for a 68040/060, more for a fast one, and its best quality when an MHI driver decodes MP3 (Settings > Sound). On a fast Amiga, or with MHI, turning off Settings > Networking > Plex > Request lower quality audio plays MP3 files as stored, and on a fast Amiga FLAC files too where flacdec.library is installed; other formats are converted either way. Settings > Networking > Plex > Plex turns it all off.
; main.c:10132
MSG_2FBD9CB6 (800955574//)
Finding a server: Settings > Networking > Plex > Plex server asks the network (Plex's GDM); choose one and it is kept. Or set its address from the Shell: SetEnv SAVE AmigaMCE/PlexServer 192.168.1.10:32400
; main.c:10136
MSG_6A05B8D3 (1778759891//)
Signing in: a server asks for its owner's token. Find it in Plex Web (an item's Get Info > View XML: the X-Plex-Token in the address) and set it from the Shell: SetEnv SAVE AmigaMCE/PlexToken <token>. Signing in at plex.tv needs HTTPS (AmiSSL) and comes later.
